From d99970e57062500614054535303e0c9630f588ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:12:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the shader cache keeps no object of more than
 a quarter of it

The bridge gives libplacebo a cache of 32 MiB that is kept in a file from
one session to the next, for the GPU programs it links. libplacebo keeps
its tables there too: the gamut table of the mapping to a display is one,
24 MiB since it is made at 96x64x512. The oldest objects make room for a
new one, so the first such table took the room of the programs, and a
second one (another source gamut, or the projector's display besides the
SDR output) pushed the programs and the first table out, to be made and
written to the file again in the next video.

An object of more than a quarter of the cache (8 MiB) is no longer kept:
such a table is made again for each video (on the build machine 47 ms with
its 32 threads, 0.6 s on one core), and the programs stay. The programs of
the sessions in the diagnostics received are 41 to 178 KiB in all.

Tested on the host with the cache of the tree and libplacebo's own, three
programs of 100 KiB, a table of 3 MiB and two of 24 MiB: before, the cache
was left with one table of 24 MiB and none of the programs, and the file
with 24 MiB; now the three programs and the small table stay (3.3 MiB),
the large tables are not kept, and the file opens again with the four.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.c | 7 ++++++-
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.h | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.c
index 157ce97..3aac4d7 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.c
@@ -87,8 +87,13 @@ struct dvbridge_shader_cache *dvbridge_shader_cache_open(const char *path, size_
         return NULL;
     c->path = strdup(path ? path : "");
     c->max_bytes = max_bytes;
+    /* Hades: no object of more than a quarter of it: libplacebo keeps its tables in the cache too
+     * (the gamut table of the mapping to a display, 24 MiB at the bridge's size), and one that
+     * large took the room of the programs (the oldest objects make room) and was written to the
+     * file with them; a second one, for another source or display, would push the first out
+     * again in every video. Such a table is made again for each video instead. */
     c->cache = pl_cache_create(pl_cache_params(.log = log, .max_total_size = max_bytes,
-                                               .max_object_size = max_bytes));
+                                               .max_object_size = max_bytes / 4));
     if (!c->path || !c->cache) {
         dvbridge_shader_cache_close(c);
         return NULL;
diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.h b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.h
index cd2e524..8b61933 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.h
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_cache.h
@@ -21,8 +21,10 @@ struct dvbridge_shader_cache;
  * against the file before anything of it is taken, and libplacebo checks the checksum of each
  * entry as it takes it (an entry that does not match is left out, with the ones after it). A file
  * that does not hold is deleted. A missing or bad file is no failure: the cache starts empty.
- * max_bytes bounds what the cache holds (the oldest entries make room) and what is read.
+ * max_bytes bounds what the cache holds (the oldest entries make room) and what is read; Hades:
+ * an entry of more than a quarter of it is not kept (DVBRIDGE_SHADER_CACHE_OBJECT_QUARTER).
  * Returns NULL only when there is no memory. */
+#define DVBRIDGE_SHADER_CACHE_OBJECT_QUARTER 1
 struct dvbridge_shader_cache *dvbridge_shader_cache_open(const char *path, size_t max_bytes, pl_log log);
 /* Without saving it. The pl_cache goes with it. */
 void dvbridge_shader_cache_close(struct dvbridge_shader_cache *cache);
-- 
